{{> EmailTitle title="You Already Have an Account" }}

{{!--
  Sent when a sign-up names an address that already has an account (#9816,
  Identity's AuthenticationEmail.sendAccountAlreadyExistsEmail). The sign-up
  page tells whoever typed the address to check their email, as it tells
  everybody, so nobody learns from it whether the address has an account:
  this email, to the address, is where that is said. Nothing was created or
  changed. The likeliest sender is the owner, who forgot they had an account
  or its password, so it offers both ways back in; when, from where and on
  which device the sign-up came (Partials/RequestOriginFields.hbs) lets the
  owner tell their own from a stranger's.
--}}

{{> InfoBlock info=(concat "Someone, maybe you, tried to sign up for " (brandNameHtml) " with this email address. It already has an account, so nothing was created or changed.")}}

